      "id": "cat-2024-question-paper-(slot-2,-qa)-mldvws",
      "q": "A function ${f}$ maps the set of natural numbers to whole numbers, such that $f(xy) = f(x)f(y)+f(x)+f(y)$ for all $x,y$ and $f(p)=1$ for every prime number ${p}$. Then, the value of $f(160000)$ is",
      "options": [
        "1023",
        "4095",
        "2047",
        "8191"
      ],
      "correct": 1,
      "explain": "Let $g(x) = f(x)+1$. Then $g(xy)-1 = (g(x)-1)(g(y)-1) + (g(x)-1) + (g(y)-1) = g(x)g(y) - 1$. So, $g(xy) = g(x)g(y)$. For any prime ${p}$, $g(p)=f(p)+1=2$. $160000 = 16 \\times 10^4 = 2^4 \\times (2\\times5)^4 = 2^8 \\times 5^4$. $g(160000) = g(2^8)g(5^4) = (g(2))^8(g(5))^4 = 2^8 \\times 2^4 = 2^{12} = 4096$. So $f(160000)=g(160000)-1=4095$.",
      "exam": "CAT 2024 Question Paper (Slot 2, QA)",
